   "evidence": "The proof is `rw [extChartAt_coe, Function.comp_apply, ModelWithCorners.left_inv]`, which uses nothing about the model. Mathlib's `extChartAt_coe` (ExtChartAt.lean:439) is not `@[simp]`, so this pattern is never simp-normalised. Grepping Mathlib for `I\\.symm \\(extChartAt I` finds nothing, so no existing lemma covers it.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/Complex/ClosedUpperHalfPlane.lean",
   "fix": "Restate it for a general `I` in the TauCeti counterpart of Mathlib's `Geometry/Manifold/IsManifold/ExtChartAt.lean` (e.g. `ModelWithCorners.symm_extChartAt_apply`), tag it `@[simp]`, delete the model-specific version and update the two call sites.",
   "issue": "`closedUpperHalfPlaneModel_symm_extChartAt` is general manifold infrastructure (`I.symm (extChartAt I x y) = chartAt H x y` holds for any `ModelWithCorners`) but is stated only for the half-plane model, and it has no `@[simp]` even though it is passed by name to two `simp only` calls in `Bordered/Atlas/Transfer.lean`.",
   "line": 159
  }
 ],
